                <pb facs="0170" n="104" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg104"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/4631: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Personal Representative of the President</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-17T19:00:00-05:00">January 17, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. General strike expected first at 6 this morning, then at 11, then at 6 this
                    evening has thus far been prevented by Batista.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
